<title>JAPAN: DLR/YEN YIELDS TO MARK CROSS SALES BY TOKYO NOON.</title>
<headline>DLR/YEN YIELDS TO MARK CROSS SALES BY TOKYO NOON.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>0300 GMT	     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT</p>
<p> USD/JPY     118.26/29		  118.60-118.20</p>
<p> USD/DEM     1.8702/05		  1.8734-1.8673</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The dollar had slithered against the yen by midday in Tokyo on Friday, yielding to persistent mark selling against the yen in cross trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>The mark fell back against the yen as a Japanese life insurer sold a sizeable amount of marks, leaving banks that received the orders with mark long positions and forcing them to sell dollars for yen for hedging, said a bank dealer.</p>
</text>
